---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME } from '../config.mjs';
---
<Base title="About" description={`About ${AUTHOR_NAME}: MSc in Autism Studies and more than five years' frontline experience supporting young people with SEND in post-16 settings.`}>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About Progress &amp; Purpose</h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:1rem">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">Progress &amp; Purpose provides practical SEND transition resources, consultancy and tailored support for schools, colleges and local authorities.</p>
        <p>We help organisations make preparation for adulthood clearer, more practical and easier to implement — from reviewing existing provision to developing resources and written guidance.</p>
        <p>Progress &amp; Purpose was founded by {AUTHOR_NAME}, who holds an MSc in Autism Studies and has more than five years' frontline experience supporting young people with SEND in post-16 settings.</p>
        <blockquote class="pull-quote">
          <p>Watching my autistic brother thrive taught me what's possible with the right support — it's why I do this work.</p>
          <cite>— {AUTHOR_NAME}</cite>
        </blockquote>
        <p>Our approach is grounded in understanding the individual or organisation behind each enquiry. We take the time to understand your circumstances, identify what matters most and provide support that is purposeful, practical and focused on meaningful progress.</p>
        <h2>Our Approach</h2>
        <p>Every person, organisation and set of circumstances is different. Our approach is therefore flexible and tailored rather than one-size-fits-all.</p>
        <p>We begin by understanding your needs, priorities and goals before identifying the most appropriate way to support you. Whether you need guidance, resources, strategic input or ongoing support, our work is designed to be practical, collaborative and outcome-focused.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Understand</strong> — We listen and establish what you need.</li>
          <li><strong>Plan</strong> — We identify priorities and practical next steps.</li>
          <li><strong>Support</strong> — We provide tailored guidance and resources.</li>
          <li><strong>Progress</strong> — We focus on sustainable, meaningful outcomes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Support is written, advisory and product-based, in plain UK English and editable formats. Quotes are agreed in writing before any work begins.</p>
        <h2>Experience &amp; Credentials</h2>
        <p>Our work is informed by academic study, professional experience and a strong understanding of SEND, inclusion and the wider challenges faced by individuals, families and organisations.</p>
        <p>We bring together knowledge and practical experience to provide thoughtful, informed and accessible support, while continuing to develop our expertise through ongoing learning and professional development.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>MSc in Autism Studies</li>
          <li>More than five years' frontline experience in post-16 SEND settings</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Request a quote</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .pull-quote {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 1.5rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--terra);
  }
  .pull-quote p {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font: 500 1.4rem/1.45 var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .pull-quote cite {
    font: 700 0.95rem/1 var(--sans);
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
